# =============================================================================
# NeOps Lab - Environment Configuration
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and adjust values for your environment. docker compose
# reads .env automatically. The Makefile does NOT read it: Makefile knobs
# (CONTAINERLAB, WAIT_*_TIMEOUT, CLAB_IMAGE, SDK_DIR, ...) are plain make
# variables / environment variables — `make local-lab-up WAIT_READY_TIMEOUT=600`
# or `export`.
#
# The values shown are the compose defaults, i.e. what runs when you set nothing.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Control-plane images
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All published images live on quay.io/zebbra (private — `docker login quay.io`)
# and are amd64-only; on Apple Silicon they run under Rosetta. Every one of them
# has `pull_policy: missing` (override with NEOPS_*_PULL_POLICY), so a
# locally-built tag that is already present is used without a registry call.
# A locally-built tag has no registry host (e.g. neops-worker-sdk:latest) and is
# therefore not pullable; `make local-env-init` / `local-env-up` / `local-lab-up`
# pull with `--ignore-pull-failures`, so that is only a warning.

# CMS (neops-core). `develop` works with the lab today.
NEOPS_CMS_IMAGE=quay.io/zebbra/neops-cms-free:develop

# Workflow engine (also runs the monitor app). PINNED, not `develop`: the lab
# needs the raised per-route body limits and the /workflow-definition/publish
# API — 0.42.2-beta.3 is the first published tag with both, and quay's
# `develop` tag has lagged the branch by weeks. See README "Image
# compatibility" before changing this.
NEOPS_WORKFLOW_ENGINE_IMAGE=quay.io/zebbra/neops-workflow-engine:0.42.2-beta.3

# Web client. `develop` works with the lab today.
NEOPS_WEB_CLIENT_IMAGE=quay.io/zebbra/neops-web-client:develop

# Worker. NOTE: as of August 2026 NO published tag runs the lab — the discovery
# function block (fb.base.neops.io/global_discover_network) is not yet in a
# released neops-worker-sdk image. Build one locally from a checkout that has
# it (`make build-worker-image SDK_DIR=../neops-worker-sdk-py`) and point this
# variable at it. `make images-check` tells you whether the configured image
# can run the lab. See README "Image compatibility".
NEOPS_WORKER_SDK_IMAGE=quay.io/zebbra/neops-worker-sdk:develop
# NEOPS_WORKER_SDK_IMAGE=neops-worker-sdk:latest
